This file exists so `go:embed all:dist` has something to match.

Without it, `go build ./...` fails on a fresh checkout with "pattern all:dist: no matching files
found" — because the real contents of this directory are produced by `pnpm -r build` and are
gitignored. A Go build that first requires a JavaScript build is a hostile thing to hand
somebody, and the box handles an assets-free binary deliberately: Handler returns nil and the
API falls back to its own minimal page.
